Z||000000||rogergarrison||10-13-2001||09:39 PM||||Some guys started tailgating me after I get off freeway. Were on a hilly, twisty nice road. I took off and totally left him. slowed down for next stop sign and did it again. he was reving his little totally riced out "racer" Honda as high as it would go between shifts, but I ate him alive everytime by 1/2 mile. All his wing and decals didnt help at all. About a mile between stop signs out in the country. I could have had lunch and desert waiting for him to catch back up. Not much of a match, had him way outclassed, but fun anyway since I got ate last week by that Vette Z06.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cozmo||10-14-2001||04:10 AM||||Wow...<BR>I kinda thought you threw a dead animal at him... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I got SERIOUSLY spanked by a new Porsche last week but it was just fun watchin' him crank that puppy up...<BR>I hate to admit it, but the Z06 is one fine piece of machinery.<P>BobC||||reg||10
Z||000002||rogergarrison||10-14-2001||04:21 AM||||I dont know if he was giving me BS about the Z06 but he said his dealer is only allowed to perform routine work like plugs, filters, oil etc on the engine. Any major work and the dealer has to send the car or engine back to factory for repair. Anyone heard this?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||10-14-2001||11:38 AM||||That sounds like  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> to me.  The Z06 engine isn't that special. It's just a modded LS1.  Any dealer should be able to work on it.  What makes the Z06 so special is the total package.  Lots of changes over the standard Vette.  And I want rims that look like those for my Fiero!  That or ZR1 or Gran Sport styled wheels.  I'm all confused....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
